<BaseLayout title="About — Joshua Harper"><article class="reading"><p class="eyebrow">The person behind the tools</p><h1>Hi, I’m Joshua.</h1><p>I’m an applied AI engineer. I work across Python backends, TypeScript interfaces, agent workflows, and the infrastructure that connects them.</p><p>My background includes data and IT systems at the University of Georgia and technical analyst work at High Street Consulting: automation, accessibility review, and the practical business of making systems useful to other people.</p><h2>Work, not just demos.</h2><p>My public resume records an AI Engineer contract role at ADP beginning April 2026, working on internal developer tooling and governed agent integrations. The projects on this site are public personal and studio work—not ADP deliverables.</p><p>I like tools with visible boundaries: files you can inspect, commands you can repeat, and tests that can disagree with the agent. There’s room for stranger experiments, too—especially where code meets audio and video.</p><h2>Personal workshop. Separate studio.</h2><p>This is where I keep my own work and notes. <a href="https://fullyautomated.enterprises/">Fully Automated Enterprises</a> is the studio I founded, with a broader remit across local AI, useful tools, and machine-made media.</p><div class="text-links"><a href="/resume/">Read the full resume →</a><a href="/contact/">Write to me →</a></div><details><summary>Older pages & working preferences</summary><p>The <a href="/about/faq/">FAQ</a> and <a href="/about/no/">working boundaries</a> remain available. Earlier artifacts live in the <a href="/work/">work archive</a>.</p></details></article></BaseLayout>
